<%# ONE PLAY, SUMMARISED — the right third of the play-by-play bar, directly
    under the rail. Locals:
      play_id, play_kind, title   identify the play; title is the feed's full text
      result                      what it was, in bold white ("Interception")
      detail                      how far or what for, or nil ("45 yard pass")
      ink_team                    whose two colours the detail wears, or nil
      avatars                     up to three { name:, athlete:, team: }, most
                                  important first; a { team: } alone draws that
                                  team's emoji (a play that names nobody, a kickoff
                                  being waited for)

    CENTRED, like the rail's rows above it, so the two read as one column — and
    on the rail's own dark ground in both themes, because the detail's team ink
    is chosen to read on dark (about 2:1 on the light theme's pale card).

    THE PORTRAITS ARE OUT OF THE FLOW, floated into the space left of the words.
    If they took part in the centring, one, two or three of them would push the
    words a different distance each time. Each is 1.75rem and tucked more than
    half under the one before, the first on top: a cluster that says "these
    three", not a row of portraits. %>
<div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 min-w-0 sm:w-1/3 px-4 py-2"
     style="background: rgba(8, 10, 16, 0.82)"
     data-test="live-plays-latest" data-play-id="<%= play_id %>" data-play-kind="<%= play_kind %>"
     title="<%= title %>">
  <span class="relative inline-flex items-center max-w-full" data-test="live-plays-group">
    <span class="absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex items-center" data-test="live-plays-avatars"
          style="right: calc(100% + 0.5rem)">
      <% avatars.first(3).each_with_index do |avatar, index| %>
        <%
          team     = avatar[:team]
          athlete  = avatar[:athlete]
          name     = avatar[:name]
          portrait = athlete&.headshot_url(width: 100)
          ring     = team ? team_card_palette(team)[:accent] : "rgba(255,255,255,0.3)"
        %>
        <span class="relative h-7 w-7 rounded-full overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center <%= name ? "text-[9px] font-black" : "text-sm" %>"
              <% if name %>data-test="live-plays-avatar" data-player="<%= name %>" title="<%= athlete ? athlete.person.full_name : name %>"<% end %>
              style="z-index: <%= 3 - index %>; <%= "margin-left: -0.75rem;" unless index.zero? %> color: <%= team_card_palette(team)[:fg] %>;
                     background: <%= normalize_hex(team&.card_background) || "#3a3f4b" %>;
                     box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px <%= ring %><%= ", 0 0 0 3px rgba(8, 10, 16, 0.55)" if name %>">
          <% if portrait %>
            <img src="<%= portrait %>" alt="" class="h-full w-full object-cover object-top">
          <% elsif name %>
            <span aria-hidden="true"><%= name.scan(/[A-Z]/).first(2).join %></span>
          <% else %>
            <span aria-hidden="true"><%= team&.emoji %></span>
          <% end %>
        </span>
      <% end %>
    </span>

    <span class="min-w-0 leading-tight text-center" data-test="live-plays-words">
      <span class="block text-sm font-extrabold text-white truncate" data-test="live-plays-result"><%= result %></span>
      <% if detail %>
        <span class="inline-block max-w-full truncate text-xs font-bold" data-test="live-plays-detail"
              style="background: <%= ink_team ? team_two_tone_ink(ink_team) : "linear-gradient(90deg, #cbd5e1, #94a3b8)" %>;
                     -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; color: transparent"><%= detail %></span>
      <% end %>
    </span>
  </span>
</div>
